      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The key precursors are typically alliin, which contains the necessary sulfur groups, and another molecule that the alliinase enzyme acts upon. The rapid onset is due to the high volatility of the resulting syn-propanethial S-oxide. Because this gas readily evaporates from the cut material and is airborne, it quickly reaches the olfactory and lacrimal system, causing an immediate, strong irritant response before significant systemic absorption can occur.",
